--- body ---

## Context

The §3 capability-timeline figure (originally shipped by ticket 0219,
data filled by ticket 0223, refined through a series of revision PRs)
uses a "launch in a public commercial product" methodology
(`docs/capability-timeline.md` Date definition). Three places in
`data/capability_timeline.csv` currently do not apply that methodology
strictly. Each is a follow-up the revision pass deferred so the main
edits could ship.

## Strictness gaps to close

### 1. Stage 1 (Chat LLM) — open-weights labs

Current dates reference open-weights model releases, not consumer
chat-product launches. Under the strict consumer-product reading:

| Lab | Current date | Strict-reading candidate |
|---|---|---|
| Mistral | 2023-09-27 (Mistral 7B Instruct open-weights) | 2024-02-26 Le Chat consumer beta |
| Alibaba | 2023-08-03 (Qwen-7B open-weights) | ~2023-09 Tongyi Qianwen full public release (or earlier April 2023 invited beta) |
| DeepSeek | 2023-11-29 (DeepSeek LLM release) | chat.deepseek.com consumer launch — date not yet pinned |

Action: web search each lab's consumer chat product launch; update
`data/capability_timeline.csv` stage-1 rows; verify the figure
re-renders with the new dates and the cross-lab ordering still tells
the same story.

### 2. Stage 6 (External tool use, MCP-like) — strict MCP reading

The loose reading shipped: "MCP-like tool-use protocol" covers
Anthropic's MCP, OpenAI function calling, and equivalents. A strict
"MCP available" reading would shift dates to each lab's MCP-support
announcement (Anthropic 2024-11-25 MCP launch; OpenAI ~2025-03 Agents
SDK MCP support; Mistral / Qwen / DeepSeek dates need verification).

Action: decide whether to keep the loose reading (current default,
per the 2026-05-22 user decision logged in PR #410) or do the strict
pass. If keeping loose: close this sub-task as a no-op with the
decision recorded. If doing strict: re-research each lab's MCP-support
milestone and update the CSV / figure.

### 3. Stage 6 — code execution as an earlier tool-use surface

The "external tool use" definition is generous enough to include
sandboxed code interpreters (Python / shell / JS). Under that reading,
several labs have a stage-6 milestone *earlier* than the currently-
recorded agentic surface:

| Lab | Current stage 6 | Code-execution earlier date |
|---|---|---|
| OpenAI | 2025-01-23 Operator | 2023-07-06 ChatGPT Code Interpreter |
| Anthropic | 2024-10-22 Computer use beta | ~2024-08 Claude.ai artifacts + code execution (date needs pinning) |
| Mistral | 2025-05-27 Agents API | Le Chat Python execution (date needs pinning) |
| Alibaba | 2024-04-07 Qwen-Agent | Qwen Chat / Tongyi Python toggle (date needs pinning) |
| DeepSeek | 2024-07-25 Function Calling API | no consumer Python toggle currently |

Backdating OpenAI's stage-6 marker from 2025-01-23 to 2023-07-06 is
a ~18-month shift — visible in the figure. The cross-lab ordering in
row 6 would change.

Action: decide framing. Three options listed in the §3 discussion
that surfaced this gap:

a) Backdate stage 6 to "earliest external-tool-use surface, including
   code execution" (option recommended in the discussion).
b) Split stage 6 into 6a (code execution) and 6b (general tool surface
   / MCP).
c) Footnote: keep current dates, document code execution as a stage-6
   sub-capability whose dates would shift the OpenAI marker earlier.

## Why this ticket exists (not done in #412/#413)

The §3 revision pass focused on the framework-vs-model reframing, the
articulation restoration, the MCP-like wording, and the stage-1 label
rename. Pushing into strict-date research mid-revision would have
ballooned the scope and risked the talk-deadline freeze. Parking here
for deliberate handling.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Stage 1 dates: decision recorded (keep open-weights / shift to
      chat-product) and applied to the CSV.
- [ ] Stage 6 MCP strictness: decision recorded and applied.
- [ ] Stage 6 code execution: decision recorded; if accepted, CSV
      updated for OpenAI, Anthropic, Mistral, Alibaba; DeepSeek
      verified absent on consumer code execution.
- [ ] Figure re-rendered.
- [ ] `make slides` builds clean.
- [ ] `docs/capability-timeline.md` schema description updated for
      whatever stage-6 framing the decisions land on.
- [ ] Adherence tests still green.

## Cutoff

2026-05-22 (the date of the strictness audit). Cells flipping after
this date are a separate ticket.
